        "question_type": "single_choice",
        "question_title": "A rectangle has fixed area \\(48\\,\\text{cm}^2\\). If its length is \\(x\\,\\text{cm}\\), determine the least possible perimeter.",
        "question_instruction": "Choose one correct option.",
        "explanation": "The breadth is \\(\\frac{48}{x}\\), so \\(P=2\\left(x+\\frac{48}{x}\\right)\\). By AM-GM, \\(x+\\frac{48}{x}\\ge2\\sqrt{48}=8\\sqrt{3}\\). Therefore, \\(P_{\\min}=16\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{cm}\\).",
        "question_audio": null,
        "time_limit_seconds": 30,
